question:
Here is a small toy C program. Find the memory-safety bugs, explain the exact input that triggers each, and the exploitability consequence (crash only vs. control-flow hijack). Do not overstate.

```c
#include <string.h>
#include <stdio.h>
void copy(char *dst, const char *src) {
    strcpy(dst, src);
}
int main(int argc, char **argv) {
    char buf[64];
    if (argc < 2) return 1;
    copy(buf, argv[1]);
    printf("%s\n", buf);
    return 0;
}
```
